#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""THE SEATING HELPER.

BATCH-5 WP-O (register row 413; the charter is mission ledger entry 1596, section A). A seat that takes over an arc
does the same five things before its first act, and until this file each seat did them with scratch scripts of its
own, opened on its own session id and its own absolute root: it copied the evaluator's verdict before anything could
overwrite it, said what that verdict was, compared the predecessor's keep-table with the operator's copy, replaced
the HANDOFF head on STATUS.md, and counted the arc's stops by column. This file is those five, tracked, in the form
of the two composers beside it. It imports no sibling: each tool under tools/lam runs alone, so the clock and the one
read below are written here and again, byte for byte, in gen_brief.py.

WHAT IT READS, AND HOW. Every file by ONE short open -- read to the end, close -- with no handle kept. The evaluator
holds the admissions record, its own verdict and the live instrument capture with NO SHARING for an instant each
(tools/lam/mission-goal-check.ps1), and a reader's handle met at that instant costs that evaluation its HANDOFF head,
its reuse or -- met at the append -- the stop itself (the hook blocks until the next stop); it can never yield an
admission. So a read is short, and this tool's own open, where it meets such a hold, is tried five times 200 ms
apart and then REFUSED by name -- never read as "absent"; a kept capture that stands and is not opened is said
COULD NOT BE OPENED, a finding, and a folder where a file is looked for is said to be a folder. A LIVE VERDICT IS
READ TWICE: the write is not atomic, so two whole reads must be byte-equal, end in a line end, hold exactly one
column-0 `goal:`, one `evaluated_at:` and one `verdict:`, each with its value on its line, one `detectors:`, as
many `  - type:` entries as `detector_count:` says, and under each entry its `ok:` and its `detail:` line. Keys are
read by exact name and colon and every other line is passed over, so a key the evaluator adds later changes nothing
here.

WHAT A VERDICT IS, BY ITS BYTES. THE COLUMN is read from the OPENING of each `instrument_exit0` detail, never by a
search of the whole of it (a declined reuse quotes capture names and header values, so a search can be fed):
  REUSED          `<leaf> exited <n> (require 0). REUSED A FRESH READING, `
  FRESH           `<leaf> exited <n> (require 0). Instrument output `
  NOT_EVALUATED   `NOT EVALUATED -- hook-mode short-circuit`
  NOT_RUN         `instrument_exit0 has no 'path'`, `instrument not on disk: `, `detector 'instrument_exit0' THREW and
                  is recorded as FAILED, not skipped: `, or `<leaf> NOT RUN: engine down -- `
  NONE            the verdict holds no such entry;  UNREAD  an entry whose detail opens as none of these;
  MIXED           two or more entries that do not share one column.
`<leaf>` is the instrument's file name -- a text that holds no path separator, no ` -- ` and no `: ` -- standing
before the first ` exited <n> (require 0). ` that one of the two sentences follows, or before ` NOT RUN: engine down
-- `. A detail in which a text that is NO leaf -- one that holds a path separator, ` -- ` or `: ` -- stands before
a whole opening does not OPEN with it and is UNREAD. PLAIN WORDS that hold none of the three, standing before
` exited <n> (require 0). ` and one of the two sentences, or before ` NOT RUN: engine down -- `, ARE that opening,
the words its leaf: a sentence so worded is read FRESH, REUSED or NOT RUN. A leaf that itself spelled one of the
openings would be read by it, and an instrument whose own file name held ` -- ` would read UNREAD; no instrument
is named either way.
THE ARM that admitted the stop is the `verdict:` word and nothing else: HALT, AWAITING_AMENDMENT_GATE,
AWAITING_DISPATCH_GATE, HANDOFF_ADMITTED, or none (MET, NOT_MET), or GOAL_ABSENT. The lists of a lower arm are still
written under a higher verdict, and under an open HALT an eligible HANDOFF head reads `ELIGIBLE, NOT SPENT`: the
record is then expected to hold no line for that brief, and this tool says so, or names the line that does.

SUBCOMMANDS
  copy --root R --goal G --close-folder NAME [--verdict FILE] [--hand-tee LABEL] [--make-folder]
      THE SEATING COPY. Reads the verdict of G -- the first of R/.mission/goals/G.verdict.yaml and
      R/.mission-runtime/lam/goals/G.verdict.yaml that stands; both standing is REFUSED unless --verdict names one --
      and writes, by exclusive create under R/.mission-runtime/lam/close/NAME/, the very bytes read, named by what
      the bytes are: G.verdict.<evaluated_at without - and :>.<VERDICT>.instrument-<COLUMN>.yaml (with --hand-tee,
      `hand-tee-<LABEL>.` stands before the stamp), and beside it <copy>.seated, ONE line, this tool's clock at the
      write. The statement `read` prints is read BEFORE the first write and printed after it; the pair is written
      whole or not at all (what this run created is taken back where a create fails, and the line says so; a copy
      ANOTHER run wrote between this run's look and its write is refused as a copy that stands, and nothing of that
      run's is touched). --make-folder first makes the ONE folder close/NAME where it is absent. REFUSED: a name
      that begins HALT- in any letter case once its dots and blanks are dropped (the evaluator's HALT scan is by
      name, and by the 8.3 name too) -- the copy's, and the close folder's NAME too, which the scan of files does
      not list and this tool neither makes nor writes into; a goal id that holds `hand-tee-` (the census tells a
      hand tee by the copy's name holding it, and a copy's name opens with its goal); a verdict whose own `goal:`
      line names another goal than G (the name is composed from the bytes, the goal among them); --hand-tee where
      the verdict's own short_circuited is above 0
      (the bytes show a hook stop, and the name is the one record of hook or hand); a copy, or a stamp without its
      copy, already standing.
  read --root R (--goal G | --verdict FILE)
      THE STATEMENT, writing nothing: the verdict word and its stamp; one COLUMN line per instrument entry (for a
      REUSED one the kept capture's path and sha256, and whether it is ON DISK under R at that digest -- read by its
      tail beyond the verdict's own mission_root, never by its absolute spelling, and not at all where that tail
      would leave R); the ARM with what stands behind it; and the HANDOFF head's reading where the goal declares
      the arm. Exit 1 where a finding stands -- among them a detail that names another kept path than the list's.
  keep --brief B --copy DIR [--exclude NAME]...
      THE OPERATOR's COMPARE, in his words: the keep-table rows of B (`| name | bytes | sha256 |`, found as his own
      line finds them: B read as UTF-32 or UTF-16 where it opens on that mark and as UTF-8 otherwise, a leading mark
      set aside, a line ended by CR LF, by LF or by a lone CR, the pattern without regard to letter case) against the
      files of DIR; `MISMATCH <name>` per failing row with a `why:` line beneath; then `<ok> of <rows>, <bad>
      mismatches`. A `.` part of a name is passed over; a name with a drive, a leading separator or a `..` part
      does not stay inside the copy and is a MISMATCH -- THERE THE VERB IS STRICTER THAN HIS LINE, which follows
      such a name where it leads. A file of the copy the system marks HIDDEN is a MISMATCH, as it is to his line,
      whose Get-Item does not see it. An --exclude is the bare name of ONE top-level folder of DIR, and one that names
      none is REFUSED.
  head --root R --line-file F (--replace-handoff | --place-handoff) [--predecessor-brief B] [--expect-sha256 S]
      THE STATUS HEAD. Prepends the lines of F to R/.mission-runtime/lam/STATUS.md and leaves every prior byte
      beneath them. The lines are the caller's bytes but for THREE tokens this tool fills from its own clock at the
      write: {CLOCKMS}, and {SEAM_FROM_FIRST} and {SEAM_FROM_END} -- the spans from the two stamps of the line
      `SEAM BASES first <stamp> end <stamp>` in the brief --predecessor-brief names. --replace-handoff is the
      successor's: line 1 must begin HANDOFF, the head found is SAID (in the form or out of it; its brief re-hashed,
      or why it is no file) and replaced either way, and the new line 1 may begin neither HANDOFF nor AWAITING.
      --place-handoff is the outgoing seat's: the new line 1 must be a HANDOFF head in the evaluator's own form,
      holding no token, whose two digests are the brief's, re-hashed -- the brief a FILE: a device's name, which
      reads as no bytes, is REFUSED. The write is ONE temporary file of one fixed
      name beside STATUS.md and ONE replace; the admissions record is opened for reading alone. Exit 3 where the
      replace was made and STATUS.md could not then be re-read and proved. TWO LIMITS of "as the evaluator reads
      it": line 1 is read as UTF-8 (a UTF-8 mark passed over), so a STATUS.md that opens with a UTF-16 mark, which
      the evaluator decodes, is here no HANDOFF head and is REFUSED; and a record line is compared key by key only
      where it parses as JSON here with the two keys in their own letter case, and searched as text otherwise --
      a line PowerShell parses and Python does not can read SPENT here and unspent there.
  census --root R --prefix P [--machine]
      THE STOPS BY COLUMN: every *.verdict*.yaml directly inside each folder of R/.mission-runtime/lam/close whose
      name starts with P (as spelled: the match is by letter case), classed by its bytes; A STOP IS ONE VERDICT's
      BYTES -- the same bytes met again, one verdict copied into two folders, are counted ONCE under the first copy
      met and the other is named (`THE SAME VERDICT AGAIN, counted once: ...`); hook stop or hand tee by the file
      name holding `hand-tee-` (it is recorded nowhere else) -- and where the copies of ONE verdict are named both
      ways, that is a FINDING: the stop is counted as its first copy says and its seconds leave the sum; the
      table, the count line, and the seconds the REUSED hook stops saved -- the first
      elapsed_seconds on the first column-0 TALLY line of each kept capture a REUSED hook stop cites, every one of
      a stop whose instrument entries are ALL reused; a stop whose entries differ is counted MIXED and not summed,
      and a stop with a FINDING -- its capture absent, differing, held, without such a line, or named otherwise by
      its own detail -- is counted and its seconds are left out.

REFUSALS are one column-0 line, "REFUSED: <reasons> -- nothing was written", exit 2, before a byte is written. Four
end on their own words in place of those: copy's two -- where the pair could not both be written (what it created
is removed, or named as standing), and where another run wrote the copy between this run's look and its write
(`this run wrote no file`, and a folder this run made is said to stand) -- and head's two after its temporary file
was written -- STATUS.md moved, or could not be replaced -- which say STATUS.md was not touched and whether the
temporary file was removed.
FINDINGS (a mismatch, a kept capture absent, differing or not opened, a detail that names another kept path than the
list's, a record line where none is expected, one verdict's bytes named a hook stop here and a hand tee there) are
printed and exit 1. No flag carries a time, and no verb takes or holds a session's id. It runs no git and starts no
process.
"""
import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import sys
import time

STATUS_PARTS = (".mission-runtime", "lam", "STATUS.md")
RECORD_PARTS = (".mission-runtime", "lam", "handoff-admissions.jsonl")
CLOSE_PARTS = (".mission-runtime", "lam", "close")
VERDICT_PLACES = ((".mission", "goals"), (".mission-runtime", "lam", "goals"))
TEMP_NAME = "STATUS.md.seat.tmp"
# The evaluator's own pattern, as its source spells it (.NET); compiled after the two substitutions Python's
# dialect needs: `(?<` to `(?P<`, and `\z` to `\Z`.
HANDOFF_HEAD_PATTERN = r"\AHANDOFF AT (?<ctx>0|[1-9][0-9]?|100)% (?<lf>[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}); (?<raw>[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}) (?<path>\S.*)\z"
HANDOFF_HEAD_RX = re.compile(HANDOFF_HEAD_PATTERN.replace("(?<", "(?P<").replace("\\z", "\\Z"))
TOKEN_RX = re.compile(r"\A[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*\Z")
STAMP_RX = re.compile(r"\A[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}\.[0-9]{3}Z\Z")
VERDICT_WORD_RX = re.compile(r"\A[A-Z][A-Z_]*\Z")
KEY_RX = re.compile(r"\A([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*):(.*)\Z")
KEEP_ROW_RX = re.compile(r"^\| (\S.*?) \| (\d+) \| ([0-9a-f]{64}) \|$", re.IGNORECASE)
LINE_TOKEN_RX = re.compile(r"\{([A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*)\}")
CLOCK_TOKENS = ("CLOCKMS", "SEAM_FROM_FIRST", "SEAM_FROM_END")
SEAM_BASES_RX = re.compile(r"\ASEAM BASES first (\S+) end (\S+)\Z")
EXITED_RX = re.compile(r"\A exited (-?[0-9]+) \(require 0\)\. (REUSED A FRESH READING, |Instrument output )")
NOT_EVALUATED_OPEN = "NOT EVALUATED -- hook-mode short-circuit"
ENGINE_DOWN = " NOT RUN: engine down -- "
NO_LEAF_RX = re.compile(r"[\\/]| -- |: ")
NOT_RUN_OPENS = ("instrument_exit0 has no 'path'", "instrument not on disk: ",
                 "detector 'instrument_exit0' THREW and is recorded as FAILED, not skipped: ")
KEPT_AT_RX = re.compile(r" THE CAPTURE CITED IS KEPT at (.+?) \((?:written now|already kept, the same bytes)")
KEPT_ITEM_RX = re.compile(r"\A(.+) sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64})\Z")
ADMITTED_LINE_RX = re.compile(r"HANDOFF ADMITTED (?:0|[1-9][0-9]?|100)% ([0-9a-f]{64}); ([0-9a-f]{64}) ")
RECORDED_AT_RX = re.compile(r" -- recorded at (.+) line ([0-9]+); the same brief never admits again")
ELAPSED_RX = re.compile(r"elapsed_seconds=([0-9]+)")
CENSUS_HEADER = ("| evaluated_at | goal | verdict | column | what | copy (folder under close/ : name, bytes, sha256) | "
                 "kept capture where REUSED |")
CENSUS_RULE = "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|"
COLUMN_SHOWN = {"REUSED": "REUSED", "FRESH": "FRESH", "NOT_EVALUATED": "NOT EVALUATED", "NOT_RUN": "NOT RUN",
                "NONE": "NONE", "UNREAD": "UNREAD", "MIXED": "MIXED"}


HELD = ("could not be opened in five tries 200 ms apart (PermissionError: another process holds it without sharing, or "
        "it is not a file this process may open); it is not read as absent")


class Refused(Exception):
    """A refusal: its reasons, and the tail its one line ends on -- "nothing was written" unless the verb says other."""

    def __init__(self, reasons, tail=None):
        Exception.__init__(self, "; ".join(reasons))
        self.reasons = list(reasons)
        self.tail = tail


def emit(text):
    """One line on stdout, ASCII whatever the console's code page: anything else is backslash-escaped."""
    sys.stdout.write(text.encode("ascii", "backslashreplace").decode("ascii") + "\n")
    sys.stdout.flush()


def clock_now():
    """The clock at the call, UTC, YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ: the form of the evaluator's evaluated_at."""
    now = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)
    return now.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.") + "%03dZ" % (now.microsecond // 1000)


def read_whole(path):
    """Every byte of one file by ONE short open: read to the end, close. An open another process refuses is tried
    five times 200 ms apart and then raised; no handle outlives the call."""
    last = None
    for attempt in range(5):
        if attempt:
            time.sleep(0.2)
        try:
            with open(path, "rb") as handle:
                return handle.read()
        except PermissionError as exc:
            last = exc
    raise last


def sha256(data):
    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()


def stamp_ms(stamp):
    """Milliseconds since the epoch of a stamp in the clock's form, or None where it is not one."""
    if not STAMP_RX.match(stamp):
        return None
    try:
        whole = datetime.datetime.strptime(stamp[:19], "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S").replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return int(whole.timestamp()) * 1000 + int(stamp[20:23])


def span_text(from_ms, to_ms):
    """A span between two stamps AS PRINTED, in the seats' form: `2 min 29.795 s (149.795 s)`."""
    milli = to_ms - from_ms
    minutes = milli // 60000
    rest = milli - minutes * 60000
    return "%d min %d.%03d s (%d.%03d s)" % (minutes, rest // 1000, rest % 1000, milli // 1000, milli % 1000)


def lf_blob_sha256(data):
    """The evaluator's LF/blob digest (Get-PlacementLfBlobSha256): bytes git's own text test calls binary -- a NUL,
    a lone CR, more non-printable than printable >> 7 -- or bytes with no CR LF pair hash AS THEY ARE; otherwise
    every CR LF is folded to LF and the rest is hashed."""
    nul = lone_cr = crlf = printable = non_printable = 0
    index, count = 0, len(data)
    while index < count:
        byte = data[index]
        if byte == 13:
            if index + 1 < count and data[index + 1] == 10:
                crlf += 1
                index += 2
            else:
                lone_cr += 1
                index += 1
            continue
        index += 1
        if byte == 10:
            continue
        if byte == 127:
            non_printable += 1
        elif byte < 32:
            if byte in (8, 9, 27, 12):
                printable += 1
            else:
                if byte == 0:
                    nul += 1
                non_printable += 1
        else:
            printable += 1
    if count >= 1 and data[count - 1] == 26:
        non_printable -= 1
    binary = lone_cr > 0 or nul > 0 or (printable >> 7) < non_printable
    if binary or crlf == 0:
        return sha256(data)
    return sha256(data.replace(b"\r\n", b"\n"))


def text_lines(data):
    """The lines of a file: bytes split on LF, one trailing CR dropped from each; the piece after a final LF is
    not a line."""
    pieces = data.decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\n")
    if pieces and pieces[-1] == "":
        pieces.pop()
    return [piece[:-1] if piece.endswith("\r") else piece for piece in pieces]


def brief_lines(data):
    """The lines of a brief AS THE OPERATOR's COMPARE LINE READS THEM (Select-String): UTF-32 or UTF-16 where the
    file opens on that mark (the UTF-32 marks looked for first: the little-endian one begins as UTF-16's does),
    else UTF-8 with a leading mark set aside; and a line ends at CR LF, at LF, and at a lone CR."""
    if data[:4] in (b"\xff\xfe\x00\x00", b"\x00\x00\xfe\xff"):
        text = data.decode("utf-32", "replace")
    elif data[:2] in (b"\xff\xfe", b"\xfe\xff"):
        text = data.decode("utf-16", "replace")
    else:
        text = data.decode("utf-8-sig", "replace")
    return re.split(r"\r\n|\n|\r", text)


def unquote(value):
    """A verdict's scalar as written: a single-quoted one unquoted (a doubled quote is one), a bare one as it is."""
    value = value.strip()
    if len(value) >= 2 and value.startswith("'") and value.endswith("'"):
        return value[1:-1].replace("''", "'")
    return value


def cut(text, most=300):
    return text if len(text) <= most else text[:most] + " ...[cut; %d characters]" % len(text)


def id_fault(label, value):
    """Why an id may not be composed into a path, or ''."""
    if not TOKEN_RX.match(value):
        return label + " " + ascii(value) + " is not one token [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*"
    return ""


def halt_named(name):
    """True where the evaluator's HALT scan would list a file of this name. The scan is by NAME, without regard to
    case; and on a volume that keeps 8.3 names it matches the SHORT name too, which the file system builds from the
    long one with its dots and blanks removed -- so `HA.LT-x.verdict...yaml` is listed as `HALT-X~1.YAM`."""
    return re.sub(r"[ .]", "", name).upper().startswith("HALT-")


def parse_verdict(data):
    """A verdict artifact by its lines: column-0 scalars and lists by exact key, and the detector entries. A key met
    twice keeps its FIRST reading and is counted."""
    lines = text_lines(data)
    verdict = {"scalars": {}, "lists": {}, "counts": {}, "detectors": []}
    index, count = 0, len(lines)
    while index < count:
        line = lines[index]
        if line.startswith("  - type: "):
            entry = {"type": line[10:].strip(), "ok": "", "detail": None}
            index += 1
            while index < count and lines[index].startswith("    "):
                if lines[index].startswith("    ok: "):
                    entry["ok"] = lines[index][8:].strip()
                elif lines[index].startswith("    detail: ") and entry["detail"] is None:
                    entry["detail"] = unquote(lines[index][12:])
                index += 1
            verdict["detectors"].append(entry)
            continue
        found = KEY_RX.match(line)
        index += 1
        if not found:
            continue
        key, rest = found.group(1), found.group(2).strip()
        verdict["counts"][key] = verdict["counts"].get(key, 0) + 1
        if rest == "" or rest.startswith("#"):
            items = []
            while index < count and lines[index].startswith("  - ") and not lines[index].startswith("  - type: "):
                items.append(unquote(lines[index][4:]))
                index += 1
            verdict["lists"].setdefault(key, items)
        elif rest == "[]" or rest.startswith("[] "):
            verdict["lists"].setdefault(key, [])
        else:
            verdict["scalars"].setdefault(key, rest)
    return verdict


def verdict_faults(data, verdict):
    """Why these bytes are not ONE whole verdict artifact a copy can be named from."""
    faults = []
    if not data.endswith(b"\n"):
        faults.append("it does not end in a line end (a half file: the evaluator's write is not atomic)")
    scalars = verdict["scalars"]
    # `goal:` with them: every writer of the artifact writes it, and a copy's name is composed from it.
    for key in ("goal", "evaluated_at", "verdict"):
        if verdict["counts"].get(key, 0) != 1:
            faults.append("it holds %d column-0 `%s:` line(s), not one" % (verdict["counts"].get(key, 0), key))
        elif key not in scalars:
            # The line stands and carries nothing after its colon (or a list): it is no goal, no stamp, no word.
            faults.append("its `%s:` line carries no value" % key)
    if "evaluated_at" in scalars and not STAMP_RX.match(scalars["evaluated_at"]):
        faults.append("its evaluated_at " + ascii(scalars["evaluated_at"]) + " is not YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ")
    if "verdict" in scalars and not VERDICT_WORD_RX.match(scalars["verdict"]):
        faults.append("its verdict " + ascii(scalars["verdict"]) + " is not one word of capitals")
    declared = scalars.get("detector_count", "")
    if not re.match(r"\A[0-9]+\Z", declared):
        faults.append("it holds no `detector_count:` that is a number")
    elif int(declared) != len(verdict["detectors"]):
        faults.append("it holds %d `  - type:` entr%s where detector_count says %s (a half file)"
                      % (len(verdict["detectors"]), "y" if len(verdict["detectors"]) == 1 else "ies", declared))
    # `detectors:` is the last key every writer of the artifact writes, and an entry is three lines: a file cut
    # short at a line end before either is whole is a half file too.
    if verdict["counts"].get("detectors", 0) != 1:
        faults.append("it holds %d column-0 `detectors:` line(s), not one (a half file)" % verdict["counts"].get("detectors", 0))
    half = [entry["type"] for entry in verdict["detectors"] if entry["ok"] == "" or entry["detail"] is None]
    if half:
        faults.append("its entry `" + half[0] + "` lacks its `ok:` or its `detail:` line (a half file)")
    return faults


def read_verdict(path, twice):
    """(bytes, parsed). REFUSED where the file is absent, held, read twice with two results, or not a whole verdict."""
    if os.path.isdir(path):
        raise Refused(["a folder stands at " + path + " where a verdict is looked for"])
    try:
        data = read_whole(path)
        again = read_whole(path) if twice else data
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise Refused(["no verdict stands at " + path])
    except PermissionError:
        raise Refused(["the verdict at " + path + " " + HELD])
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise Refused(["the verdict at " + path + " cannot be read (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ")"])
    if again != data:
        raise Refused(["the verdict at " + path + " read twice gave two results (%d B, then %d B): an evaluation is "
                       "writing it" % (len(data), len(again))])
    verdict = parse_verdict(data)
    faults = verdict_faults(data, verdict)
    if faults:
        raise Refused(["the file at " + path + " is not one whole verdict: " + "; ".join(faults)])
    return data, verdict


def read_optional(path, what):
    """The bytes of a file that may be absent (None then). A folder at the path, and an open that is refused past the
    five tries, are REFUSED by name: neither is read as absent."""
    if os.path.isdir(path):
        raise Refused(["a folder stands at " + path + " where the " + what + " is looked for"])
    try:
        return read_whole(path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except PermissionError:
        raise Refused(["the " + what + " at " + path + " " + HELD])
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        raise Refused(["the " + what + " at " + path + " cannot be read (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ")"])


def hidden(path):
    """True where the system marks the file hidden (Windows' attribute); False where it keeps no mark."""
    try:
        return bool(getattr(os.stat(path), "st_file_attributes", 0) & 2)
    except OSError:
        return False


def read_file(path, what):
    """The bytes of a file that must stand: its absence is REFUSED by name, as a hold is."""
    data = read_optional(path, what)
    if data is None:
        raise Refused(["no " + what + " at " + path])
    return data


def classify(detail):
    """(column, exit or None) of ONE instrument_exit0 detail, by its opening."""
    if detail is None:
        return "UNREAD", None
    if detail.startswith(NOT_EVALUATED_OPEN):
        return "NOT_EVALUATED", None
    for opening in NOT_RUN_OPENS:
        if detail.startswith(opening):
            return "NOT_RUN", None
    # AN OPENING BEGINS WITH A LEAF: a text that holds no path separator, no ` -- ` and no `: `. The leaf is what
    # stands before ` NOT RUN: engine down -- ` where that comes before any ` exited `; else before the FIRST
    # ` exited ` that the whole opening follows -- ` exited <n> (require 0). ` and one of the two sentences. Where
    # what stands before is no leaf, the detail OPENS otherwise and is UNREAD: a whole opening quoted further on in
    # another sentence is not the detail's opening.
    at = detail.find(" exited ")
    down = detail.find(ENGINE_DOWN)
    if down > 0 and (at < 0 or down < at) and not NO_LEAF_RX.search(detail[:down]):
        return "NOT_RUN", None
    while at > 0 and not NO_LEAF_RX.search(detail[:at]):
        found = EXITED_RX.match(detail[at:])
        if found:
            return ("REUSED" if found.group(2).startswith("REUSED") else "FRESH"), int(found.group(1))
        at = detail.find(" exited ", at + 1)
    return "UNREAD", None


def instrument_entries(verdict):
    """One reading per instrument_exit0 entry: its column, exit, detail and -- where REUSED -- the kept copy the
    verdict names for it (the path and sha256 from `instrument_captures_kept`, matched to the detail's own path)."""
    kept = []
    for item in verdict["lists"].get("instrument_captures_kept", []):
        found = KEPT_ITEM_RX.match(item)
        if found:
            kept.append((found.group(1), found.group(2)))
    readings = []
    reused = [entry for entry in verdict["detectors"] if entry["type"] == "instrument_exit0"
              and classify(entry["detail"])[0] == "REUSED"]
    for entry in verdict["detectors"]:
        if entry["type"] != "instrument_exit0":
            continue
        column, code = classify(entry["detail"])
        reading = {"column": column, "exit": code, "detail": entry["detail"] or "", "kept_path": None,
                   "kept_sha": None, "kept_note": "", "kept_said": None}
        if column == "REUSED":
            said = KEPT_AT_RX.search(reading["detail"])
            # The path the detail names: what stands between `KEPT at ` and the parenthesis -- less a digest, where
            # a wording of the evaluator's writes ` sha256 <64 hex>` after the path, so that a detail which names
            # the list's own path is never read as naming another.
            said_path = None if said is None else re.sub(r" sha256 [0-9a-f]{64}\Z", "", said.group(1))
            chosen = None
            if said_path is not None:
                for path, digest in kept:
                    if os.path.normcase(path) == os.path.normcase(said_path):
                        chosen = (path, digest)
                        break
            if chosen is None and len(kept) == 1 and len(reused) == 1:
                # ONE reused entry and ONE item: the item is taken. Where the entry's own detail names ANOTHER path
                # the verdict contradicts itself about which capture was kept, and that is a finding.
                chosen = kept[0]
                if said_path is not None:
                    reading["kept_said"] = said_path
                    reading["kept_note"] = " -- BUT THE DETAIL NAMES ANOTHER PATH, " + said_path + ": a finding"
            if chosen is not None:
                reading["kept_path"], reading["kept_sha"] = chosen
        readings.append(reading)
    return readings


def column_word(readings):
    """The column a copy is NAMED by."""
    if not readings:
        return "NONE"
    words = sorted({reading["column"] for reading in readings})
    return words[0] if len(words) == 1 else "MIXED"


def kept_on_disk(root, verdict, kept_path, kept_sha):
    """(word, local path or '', bytes or None) -- EQUAL, ABSENT, DIFFERS, COULD NOT BE OPENED, NOT A FILE, or NOT
    UNDER mission_root. The kept copy is read under --root by its tail beyond the verdict's own mission_root, never
    by its absolute spelling; a tail that climbs out by `..`, or holds a colon (a drive, a stream), is not read at
    all. COULD NOT BE OPENED is said of ONE thing: a file that stands and that five tries did not open (a hold).
    A folder at the path, and a path the system refuses for any other reason (a name no file can bear), are NOT A
    FILE, with the reason; none of the three is read as absent."""
    base = verdict["scalars"].get("mission_root", "")
    norm_base = os.path.normcase(base.rstrip("\\/"))
    norm_path = os.path.normcase(kept_path)
    if not norm_base or not (norm_path.startswith(norm_base + "\\") or norm_path.startswith(norm_base + "/")):
        return "NOT UNDER mission_root", "", None
    parts = [part for part in re.split(r"[\\/]", kept_path[len(base.rstrip("\\/")) + 1:]) if part]
    if not parts or any(part in (".", "..") or ":" in part for part in parts):
        return "NOT UNDER mission_root", "", None
    local = os.path.join(root, *parts)
    if not os.path.normcase(os.path.abspath(local)).startswith(os.path.normcase(os.path.abspath(root)).rstrip("\\/") + os.sep):
        return "NOT UNDER mission_root", "", None
    if os.path.isdir(local):
        return "NOT A FILE (a folder stands there)", local, None
    try:
        data = read_whole(local)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return "ABSENT", local, None
    except PermissionError:
        return "COULD NOT BE OPENED", local, None
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        return "NOT A FILE (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ": the system refuses that path)", local, None
    return ("EQUAL" if sha256(data) == kept_sha else "DIFFERS"), local, data


def record_find(record, lf_digest, raw_digest):
    """(digest found, line number) by the evaluator's own rule, or (None, 0): a line that parses and holds the two
    keys is compared key by key; any other line is searched as text."""
    for number, line in enumerate(record.decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\n"), start=1):
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        try:
            obj = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            obj = None
        if isinstance(obj, dict) and "brief_lf_sha256" in obj and "brief_working_sha256" in obj:
            for value in (str(obj["brief_lf_sha256"]).lower(), str(obj["brief_working_sha256"]).lower()):
                if value and value in (lf_digest, raw_digest):
                    return value, number
        else:
            low = line.lower()
            for value in (lf_digest, raw_digest):
                if value and value in low:
                    return value, number
    return None, 0


def record_lines(record):
    return len([line for line in record.split(b"\n") if line.strip()])


def statement(verdict, root):
    """(lines, findings): what a verdict is, by its bytes. `root` is where the runtime plane it names is read."""
    scalars = verdict["scalars"]
    word = scalars["verdict"]
    out = ["VERDICT " + word + " evaluated_at " + scalars["evaluated_at"],
           "goal_file: " + scalars.get("goal_file", "(the verdict carries none)")]
    findings = 0
    readings = instrument_entries(verdict)
    if not readings:
        out.append("COLUMN NONE (the verdict holds no instrument_exit0 entry)")
    for reading in readings:
        column = reading["column"]
        if column == "REUSED":
            if reading["kept_path"] is None:
                out.append("COLUMN REUSED exit %d kept: THE VERDICT NAMES NO KEPT COPY for it under "
                           "instrument_captures_kept -- a finding" % reading["exit"])
                findings += 1
                continue
            state, _, _ = kept_on_disk(root, verdict, reading["kept_path"], reading["kept_sha"])
            if state == "COULD NOT BE OPENED":
                state += " (it stands, and five tries 200 ms apart did not open it: it is not read as absent)"
            out.append("COLUMN REUSED exit %d kept %s sha256 %s on disk: %s%s" % (
                reading["exit"], reading["kept_path"], reading["kept_sha"], state, reading["kept_note"]))
            if state != "EQUAL" or reading["kept_note"]:
                findings += 1
        elif column == "FRESH":
            out.append("COLUMN FRESH exit %d" % reading["exit"])
        elif column == "NOT_EVALUATED":
            out.append("COLUMN NOT EVALUATED (" + cut(reading["detail"][len(NOT_EVALUATED_OPEN):].lstrip(": ")) + ")")
        elif column == "NOT_RUN":
            out.append("COLUMN NOT RUN (" + cut(reading["detail"]) + ")")
        else:
            out.append("COLUMN UNREAD (" + cut(reading["detail"]) + ")")
    handoff = [entry for entry in verdict["detectors"] if entry["type"] == "handoff_brief_present"]
    handoff_detail = (handoff[0]["detail"] or "") if handoff else ""
    record_path = os.path.join(root, *RECORD_PARTS)
    if word == "HALT":
        out.append("ARM HALT open_halts: " + (", ".join(verdict["lists"].get("open_halts", [])) or "(none named)"))
    elif word in ("AWAITING_AMENDMENT_GATE", "AWAITING_DISPATCH_GATE"):
        lines = verdict["lists"].get(word.lower(), [])
        out.append("ARM %s %d line(s): %s" % (word, len(lines), " ; ".join(lines) or "(none named)"))
    elif word == "HANDOFF_ADMITTED":
        recorded = RECORDED_AT_RX.search(handoff_detail)
        digests = ADMITTED_LINE_RX.search(" ".join(verdict["lists"].get("handoff_admitted", [])) or handoff_detail)
        if handoff_detail.startswith("ADMITTED BY HAND, NOT RECORDED"):
            out.append("ARM HANDOFF_ADMITTED BY HAND, NOT RECORDED")
        elif recorded and digests:
            number = int(recorded.group(2))
            record = read_optional(record_path, "admissions record")
            lines = [] if record is None else record.decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\n")
            carried = 1 <= number <= len(lines) and any(value in lines[number - 1].lower() for value in digests.groups())
            if carried:
                out.append("ARM HANDOFF_ADMITTED recorded at line %d (the record re-read under --root: that line "
                           "carries the brief's digests %s / %s)" % (number, digests.group(1)[:8], digests.group(2)[:8]))
            else:
                out.append("ARM HANDOFF_ADMITTED recorded at line %d -- BUT THE RECORD RE-READ UNDER --root %s: a finding"
                           % (number, "IS ABSENT" if record is None else "HOLDS NO SUCH LINE CARRYING THE BRIEF's DIGESTS"))
                findings += 1
        else:
            out.append("ARM HANDOFF_ADMITTED (how, the bytes do not say: " + cut(handoff_detail, 160) + ")")
    elif word == "GOAL_ABSENT":
        out.append("ARM GOAL_ABSENT")
    elif word == "NOT_MET":
        failing = [entry["type"] for entry in verdict["detectors"]
                   if entry["ok"] == "false" and not (entry["detail"] or "").startswith(NOT_EVALUATED_OPEN)]
        if "evaluator_error" in scalars:
            maker = "evaluator_error: " + cut(unquote(scalars["evaluator_error"]), 200)
        elif "goal_parse_error" in scalars:
            maker = "goal_parse_error: " + cut(unquote(scalars["goal_parse_error"]), 200)
        elif handoff_detail.startswith("NOT ADMITTED -- the admissions record"):
            maker = "the admission's append failed"
        elif failing:
            maker = "failing: " + ", ".join(failing)
        else:
            maker = "no failing entry is named in the bytes"
        out.append("ARM none: NOT_MET (" + maker + ")")
    elif word == "MET":
        out.append("ARM none: MET")
    else:
        out.append("ARM " + word + " (a verdict word this tool does not know)")
    short = re.match(r"\A([0-9]+)", scalars.get("short_circuited", ""))
    if short and int(short.group(1)) > 0:
        out.append("A HOOK STOP (short_circuited %s)" % short.group(1))
    else:
        out.append("hook or hand: not in the bytes")
    if handoff:
        if handoff_detail.startswith("no HANDOFF head"):
            out.append("no HANDOFF head")
        elif handoff_detail.startswith("HANDOFF head NOT admitted -- "):
            out.append("HANDOFF head REFUSED: " + cut(handoff_detail[len("HANDOFF head NOT admitted -- "):], 400))
        elif handoff_detail.startswith("ELIGIBLE, NOT SPENT -- "):
            digests = ADMITTED_LINE_RX.search(handoff_detail)
            under = "HALT" if word == "HALT" else "an AWAITING line" if word.startswith("AWAITING") else word
            record = read_optional(record_path, "admissions record")
            if digests is None:
                out.append("HANDOFF head ELIGIBLE, NOT SPENT; its digests are not in the detail, so the record was not searched")
            else:
                held = 0 if record is None else record_lines(record)
                hit, number = (None, 0) if record is None else record_find(record, digests.group(1), digests.group(2))
                if hit:
                    out.append("HANDOFF head ELIGIBLE, NOT SPENT -- BUT THE ADMISSIONS RECORD CARRIES %s AT LINE %d of %d: "
                               "a finding, none is expected under %s" % (hit[:8], number, held, under))
                    findings += 1
                else:
                    out.append("HANDOFF head ELIGIBLE, NOT SPENT; the admissions record %s, none carrying %s or %s: as "
                               "expected under %s" % ("is absent" if record is None else "holds %d line(s)" % held,
                                                      digests.group(1)[:8], digests.group(2)[:8], under))
        elif handoff_detail.startswith("ADMITTED ONE STOP") or handoff_detail.startswith("ADMITTED BY HAND"):
            out.append("HANDOFF head ADMITTED")
        else:
            out.append("HANDOFF head: " + cut(handoff_detail, 300))
    return out, findings


def locate_verdict(root, goal, named):
    """The verdict file of a goal: --verdict, else the first of the two places that stands; both standing REFUSED."""
    if named:
        return os.path.abspath(named)
    places = [os.path.join(root, *(place + (goal + ".verdict.yaml",))) for place in VERDICT_PLACES]
    # Whatever stands at a place is taken as standing there: a folder of that name is then SAID to be a folder by
    # the read, as it is under --verdict, and is not told as "no verdict".
    standing = [place for place in places if os.path.lexists(place)]
    if not standing:
        raise Refused(["no verdict of " + goal + " stands at " + places[0] + " or at " + places[1]])
    if len(standing) > 1:
        raise Refused(["a verdict of " + goal + " stands at BOTH " + places[0] + " and " + places[1] +
                       ": name the one meant with --verdict"])
    return standing[0]


def run_copy(args):
    root = os.path.abspath(args.root)
    faults = [fault for fault in (id_fault("--goal", args.goal), id_fault("--close-folder", args.close_folder),
                                  id_fault("--hand-tee", args.hand_tee) if args.hand_tee is not None else "") if fault]
    if faults:
        raise Refused(faults)
    if halt_named(args.goal):
        raise Refused(["--goal " + ascii(args.goal) + " begins HALT- once its dots are dropped, in any letter case: its copy would be named " +
                       args.goal + ".verdict..., and a file whose name -- or whose 8.3 name -- begins HALT- under "
                       ".mission-runtime/lam reads as an OPEN HALT to the evaluator's scan, which is by name"])
    if "hand-tee-" in args.goal:
        # THE CENSUS TELLS A HAND TEE BY THE COPY's NAME HOLDING `hand-tee-`, and a copy's name opens with its goal:
        # every copy of such a goal, a hook stop's among them, would be counted a hand tee.
        raise Refused(["--goal " + ascii(args.goal) + " holds `hand-tee-`: a copy's name opens with its goal, and the "
                       "census tells a hand tee from a hook stop by the name holding `hand-tee-` -- every copy of this "
                       "goal would be counted a hand tee"])
    if halt_named(args.close_folder):
        # The scan lists FILES, so a folder of such a name is not read as an open HALT; it is refused all the same:
        # this tool makes and writes into no name under .mission-runtime/lam that begins HALT-, a folder's among them.
        raise Refused(["--close-folder " + ascii(args.close_folder) + " begins HALT- once its dots are dropped, in any letter "
                       "case: this tool makes no folder, and writes into none, whose name begins HALT- under "
                       ".mission-runtime/lam"])
    source = locate_verdict(root, args.goal, args.verdict)
    data, verdict = read_verdict(source, twice=True)
    # THE NAME IS COMPOSED FROM THE BYTES, the goal among them: a verdict whose own `goal:` line names another goal
    # is not copied under this one's name (--verdict may name any file).
    said_goal = verdict["scalars"].get("goal")
    if said_goal is not None and unquote(said_goal) != args.goal:
        raise Refused(["the verdict at " + source + " is goal " + ascii(unquote(said_goal)) + "'s by its own `goal:` line, "
                       "not --goal " + ascii(args.goal) + "'s: a copy is named for the goal its bytes name"])
    column = column_word(instrument_entries(verdict))
    short = re.match(r"\A([0-9]+)", verdict["scalars"].get("short_circuited", ""))
    if args.hand_tee is not None and short and int(short.group(1)) > 0:
        raise Refused(["--hand-tee is given and the verdict's own bytes show A HOOK STOP (short_circuited " + short.group(1) +
                       ", which only a Stop hook's evaluation writes above 0): a copy's name is the one record of hook or "
                       "hand, and this one would say hand"])
    compact = verdict["scalars"]["evaluated_at"].replace("-", "").replace(":", "")
    name = (args.goal + ".verdict." + ("hand-tee-" + args.hand_tee + "." if args.hand_tee is not None else "") +
            compact + "." + verdict["scalars"]["verdict"] + ".instrument-" + column + ".yaml")
    if halt_named(name):
        raise Refused(["the copy would be named " + name + ", and a file whose name -- or whose 8.3 name -- begins HALT- "
                       "under .mission-runtime/lam reads as an OPEN HALT to the evaluator's scan, which is by name"])
    if len(name) + len(".seated") > 255:
        raise Refused(["the copy would be named " + name + ", which with its stamp's `.seated` is longer than 255 characters"])
    close = os.path.join(root, *CLOSE_PARTS)
    folder = os.path.join(close, args.close_folder)
    target = os.path.join(folder, name)
    seated = target + ".seated"
    make = False
    if not os.path.isdir(folder):
        if not args.make_folder:
            raise Refused(["the close folder " + folder + " is absent (--make-folder makes that one folder)"])
        if os.path.exists(folder) or not os.path.isdir(close):
            raise Refused(["--make-folder makes the ONE folder " + folder + ", and " +
                           ("something that is not a folder stands there" if os.path.exists(folder)
                            else "its parent " + close + " is absent")])
        make = True
    elif os.path.lexists(target):
        there = read_optional(target, "copy")
        raise Refused(["a file already stands at " + target + " (the copy there " +
                       ("is BYTE-EQUAL to the verdict read" if there == data else "is NOT the bytes read") +
                       "): a seating copy is never written over"])
    elif os.path.lexists(seated):
        raise Refused(["a stamp stands at " + seated + " and NO copy beside it (" + target + " is absent): a seating "
                       "stamp is never written over"])
    # THE STATEMENT IS READ BEFORE THE FIRST WRITE: it opens the admissions record, and an open that is refused there
    # is refused while nothing is written. After the two creates nothing refuses.
    lines, findings = statement(verdict, root)
    wrote = []
    try:
        if make:
            try:
                os.mkdir(folder)
                wrote.append(folder)
            except FileExistsError:
                # ANOTHER RUN made the folder between this run's look and its write: it stands, which is all
                # --make-folder asks, and this run did not make it.
                if not os.path.isdir(folder):
                    raise
                make = False
        try:
            handle = open(target, "xb")
        except FileExistsError:
            # ANOTHER RUN wrote the copy first. Nothing of this run's is taken back, for it wrote no file -- and what
            # stands there is the other run's, so the line does not say that nothing stands.
            raise Refused(["a file already stands at " + target + ": another run wrote it between this run's look and "
                           "its write, and a seating copy is never written over"],
                          tail="this run wrote no file" + (", and the folder it made stands, holding that copy" if wrote else ""))
        with handle:
            wrote.append(target)
            handle.write(data)
        stamp = clock_now()
        with open(seated, "xb") as handle:
            wrote.append(seated)
            handle.write((stamp + "\n").encode("ascii"))
    except OSError as exc:
        # The pair is written whole or not at all: what THIS run created is taken back, the newest first.
        left = []
        for made in reversed(wrote):
            try:
                if os.path.isdir(made):
                    os.rmdir(made)
                else:
                    os.remove(made)
            except OSError:
                left.append(made)
        raise Refused(["the copy and its stamp could not both be written (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + " at " +
                       str(exc.filename or target) + ")"],
                      tail=("what this run created was removed, and nothing stands" if not left
                            else "AND THIS RUN's OWN FILE(S) COULD NOT BE REMOVED: " + ", ".join(left) + " STAND"))
    if make:
        emit("MADE the folder " + folder)
    emit("COPIED " + source + " -> " + target)
    emit("SEATED " + stamp + " -> " + seated)
    try:
        back = read_whole(target)
    except OSError as exc:
        back = None
        emit("THE COPY %d B sha256 %s, CR LF kept; re-read: NOT READ (%s)" % (len(data), sha256(data), exc.__class__.__name__))
    else:
        emit("THE COPY %d B sha256 %s, CR LF kept; re-read: %s" % (len(data), sha256(data),
                                                                  "BYTE-EQUAL" if back == data else "NOT EQUAL"))
    try:
        since = read_whole(source)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        emit("THE VERDICT FILE SINCE THE READ: GONE")
    except OSError as exc:
        emit("THE VERDICT FILE SINCE THE READ: NOT READ (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ": it is held, or cannot be opened)")
    else:
        emit("THE VERDICT FILE SINCE THE READ: " + ("UNCHANGED" if since == data else "MOVED (another evaluation wrote it)"))
    for line in lines:
        emit(line)
    if back != data:
        emit("THE COPY WAS NOT READ BACK AS WRITTEN: it stands, with its stamp")
        return 3
    return 1 if findings else 0


def run_read(args):
    root = os.path.abspath(args.root)
    if args.goal is not None:
        fault = id_fault("--goal", args.goal)
        if fault:
            raise Refused([fault])
    source = locate_verdict(root, args.goal, args.verdict)
    _, verdict = read_verdict(source, twice=True)
    emit("READ " + source)
    lines, findings = statement(verdict, root)
    for line in lines:
        emit(line)
    return 1 if findings else 0


def run_keep(args):
    brief = read_file(args.brief, "brief")
    if not os.path.isdir(args.copy):
        raise Refused(["no copy folder at " + args.copy])
    rows = [found.groups() for found in (KEEP_ROW_RX.match(line) for line in brief_lines(brief)) if found]
    if not rows:
        raise Refused(["the brief at " + args.brief + " holds no keep-table row (`| name | bytes | sha256 |`)"])
    try:
        tops = {name.lower() for name in os.listdir(args.copy) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(args.copy, name))}
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused(["the copy folder at " + args.copy + " cannot be listed (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ")"])
    stray = [given for given in (args.exclude or []) if given.lower() not in tops]
    if stray:
        raise Refused(["--exclude " + ", ".join(ascii(given) for given in stray) + " is not the bare name of a top-level "
                       "folder of " + args.copy + ": nothing would be left out, and the line would say it was"])
    excluded = {name.lower() for name in (args.exclude or [])}
    named = set()
    bad = 0
    for name, size, digest in rows:
        # A `.` part names the folder it stands in and leaves nothing: it is passed over, as his Join-Path passes it.
        parts = [part for part in re.split(r"[\\/]", name) if part not in ("", ".")]
        why = ""
        # A row is his: an upper-case digest is a row to the operator's line (Select-String, no regard to case) and
        # `sha256 differs` to his -cne. A name with a drive, a stream, a leading separator or `..` is no file of the
        # copy, and it NAMES none: the file that stands where such a name would lead is counted as not named.
        if not parts or name[0] in "\\/" or any(part == ".." or ":" in part for part in parts):
            why = "the name does not stay inside the copy"
        else:
            path = os.path.join(args.copy, *parts)
            # THE FILE a row leads to is the file it names, by the path the system opens: a name the system reads
            # more loosely than it is spelled (a trailing blank, a short 8.3 name) names the file it opens.
            named.add(os.path.normcase(os.path.realpath(path)))
            if not os.path.isfile(path):
                why = "absent"
            elif hidden(path):
                # His line's Get-Item does not see a file the system marks hidden: to it the row is a MISMATCH.
                why = "hidden: the operator's line does not see a hidden file"
            else:
                data = read_file(path, "file of the copy")
                if len(data) != int(size):
                    why = "bytes %s against %d" % (size, len(data))
                elif sha256(data) != digest:
                    why = "sha256 differs"
        if why:
            bad += 1
            emit("MISMATCH " + name)
            emit("  why: " + why)
    emit("%d of %d, %d mismatches" % (len(rows) - bad, len(rows), bad))
    unnamed = 0
    top = os.path.abspath(args.copy)
    for folder, folders, files in os.walk(top):
        if os.path.abspath(folder) == top:
            folders[:] = [inner for inner in folders if inner.lower() not in excluded]
        for name in files:
            if os.path.normcase(os.path.realpath(os.path.join(folder, name))) not in named:
                unnamed += 1
    emit("files in the copy the table does not name: %d%s" % (
        unnamed, (" (left out: " + ", ".join(sorted(excluded)) + ")") if excluded else ""))
    return 1 if bad else 0


def head_found(root, head, record):
    """What line 1 is, as the evaluator reads it: IN THE FORM (and its brief, re-hashed; SPENT or UNSPENT) or OUT."""
    found = HANDOFF_HEAD_RX.match(head)
    if not found:
        return ("LINE 1 FOUND: a HANDOFF head OUT OF THE FORM (the evaluator refuses it at every stop): " + cut(head, 200))
    lf_slot, raw_slot = found.group("lf").lower(), found.group("raw").lower()
    named = found.group("path")
    local = named.replace("/", "\\")
    # A head IN THE FORM is REPLACED whatever its path is: the evaluator reads a path that is no file as `no file`
    # and refuses that head at every stop, so this verb says so and goes on. One thing alone refuses here -- a FILE
    # that stands and that five tries do not open.
    brief, hashed = None, ""
    try:
        path = os.path.abspath(local) if os.path.isabs(local) else os.path.abspath(os.path.join(root, local))
        if os.path.isdir(path):
            hashed = "its brief CANNOT BE READ AS A FILE at " + path + " (a folder stands there)"
        elif os.path.exists(path) and not os.path.isfile(path):
            hashed = "its brief CANNOT BE READ AS A FILE at " + path + " (what stands there is no file: a device's name)"
        else:
            brief = read_whole(path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        hashed = "its brief is NOT ON DISK at " + path
    except PermissionError:
        raise Refused(["the brief at " + path + " " + HELD])
    except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
        hashed = "its brief CANNOT BE READ AS A FILE at " + cut(named, 200) + " (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ")"
    if brief is None:
        lf_now, raw_now = lf_slot, raw_slot
    else:
        lf_now, raw_now = lf_blob_sha256(brief), sha256(brief)
        hashed = "its brief re-hashed: LF/blob %s, working %s -- %s" % (
            lf_now[:8], raw_now[:8], "EITHER SLOT MATCHES" if (lf_slot == lf_now or raw_slot == raw_now) else "NEITHER SLOT MATCHES")
    hit, number = (None, 0) if record is None else record_find(record, lf_now, raw_now)
    spent = ("SPENT (the admissions record carries %s at line %d)" % (hit[:8], number)) if hit else (
        "UNSPENT (the admissions record %s)" % ("is absent" if record is None else "holds %d line(s), none carrying it" % record_lines(record)))
    return "LINE 1 FOUND: a HANDOFF head IN THE FORM -- ctx %s%%, %s; %s, path %s; %s; %s" % (
        found.group("ctx"), lf_slot[:8], raw_slot[:8], named, hashed, spent)


def run_head(args):
    root = os.path.abspath(args.root)
    status = os.path.join(root, *STATUS_PARTS)
    temp = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(status), TEMP_NAME)
    given = read_file(args.line_file, "line file")
    faults = []
    if args.expect_sha256 is not None and not re.match(r"\A[0-9A-Fa-f]{64}\Z", args.expect_sha256):
        faults.append("--expect-sha256 " + ascii(args.expect_sha256) + " is not 64 hex digits (given empty, it would "
                      "be the one check the caller asked for and did not get)")
    if not given:
        faults.append("the line file is empty")
    else:
        if b"\r" in given:
            faults.append("the line file holds a CR")
        odd = sorted({byte for byte in given if byte > 126 or (byte < 32 and byte not in (10, 13))})
        if odd:
            faults.append("the line file holds a control character or a non-ASCII byte (" +
                          ", ".join(str(byte) for byte in odd) + ")")
        if not given.endswith(b"\n"):
            faults.append("the line file does not end in LF")
        elif b"\n\n" in given or given.startswith(b"\n"):
            faults.append("the line file holds an empty line")
    if faults:
        raise Refused(faults)
    text = given.decode("ascii")
    tokens = LINE_TOKEN_RX.findall(text)
    other = sorted({token for token in tokens if token not in CLOCK_TOKENS})
    if other:
        raise Refused(["the line file holds " + ", ".join("{" + token + "}" for token in other) + ": this tool fills "
                       "{CLOCKMS}, {SEAM_FROM_FIRST} and {SEAM_FROM_END} from its own clock and no other token"])
    bases = None
    if "SEAM_FROM_FIRST" in tokens or "SEAM_FROM_END" in tokens:
        if not args.predecessor_brief:
            raise Refused(["the line file asks a seam span and no --predecessor-brief is given to read the two bases from"])
        brief_lines = text_lines(read_file(args.predecessor_brief, "brief"))
        found = [made for made in (SEAM_BASES_RX.match(line) for line in brief_lines) if made]
        if len(found) != 1:
            raise Refused(["the line file asks a seam span and the brief at " + args.predecessor_brief + " holds %d "
                           "line(s) `SEAM BASES first <stamp> end <stamp>`, not one" % len(found)])
        bases = (stamp_ms(found[0].group(1)), stamp_ms(found[0].group(2)), found[0].group(1), found[0].group(2))
        if bases[0] is None or bases[1] is None:
            raise Refused(["the SEAM BASES line of " + args.predecessor_brief + " does not hold two stamps "
                           "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmmZ"])
    if not os.path.isfile(status):
        raise Refused(["no STATUS.md at " + status])
    old = read_file(status, "STATUS.md")
    before = sha256(old)
    if args.expect_sha256 is not None and args.expect_sha256.lower() != before:
        raise Refused(["STATUS.md is sha256 " + before + ", not the --expect-sha256 given"])
    record = read_optional(os.path.join(root, *RECORD_PARTS), "admissions record")
    whole = old[3:] if old.startswith(b"\xef\xbb\xbf") else old
    first_end = whole.find(b"\n")
    head = (whole if first_end < 0 else whole[:first_end]).decode("utf-8", "replace").rstrip("\r \t")
    new_first = text.split("\n")[0]
    said = ""
    if args.replace_handoff:
        if not head.startswith("HANDOFF"):
            raise Refused(["line 1 of STATUS.md does not begin HANDOFF, so there is no HANDOFF head to replace (it reads: " +
                           cut(head, 120) + ")"])
        if new_first.startswith("HANDOFF") or new_first.startswith("AWAITING"):
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 begins " + ("HANDOFF" if new_first.startswith("HANDOFF") else "AWAITING") +
                           ": --replace-handoff places a plain head, which the evaluator reads as no HANDOFF head"])
        said = head_found(root, head, record)
    else:
        in_first = LINE_TOKEN_RX.findall(new_first)
        if in_first:
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 holds {" + in_first[0] + "}: a HANDOFF head is placed as given -- it is "
                           "checked against its brief as it stands in the line file -- and the three tokens are filled "
                           "on the lines beneath it"])
        found = HANDOFF_HEAD_RX.match(new_first)
        if not found:
            raise Refused(['the new line 1 is not in the form "HANDOFF AT <0-100>% <sha256 LF/blob>; <sha256 working> '
                           '<path of the brief>", which is the only line --place-handoff places'])
        local = found.group("path").replace("/", "\\")
        try:
            path = os.path.abspath(local) if os.path.isabs(local) else os.path.abspath(os.path.join(root, local))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 names the brief " + cut(found.group("path"), 200) + ", which is no path of a file"])
        if os.path.exists(path) and not os.path.isdir(path) and not os.path.isfile(path):
            # A device's name (NUL) reads as no bytes, whose digest any line can carry: it is no brief.
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 names the brief " + found.group("path") + ", and what stands at " + path +
                           " is no file (a device's name): a HANDOFF head is placed over a brief that is a file"])
        brief = read_optional(path, "brief")
        if brief is None:
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 names the brief " + found.group("path") + ", and no file stands at " + path])
        lf_now, raw_now = lf_blob_sha256(brief), sha256(brief)
        wrong = []
        if found.group("lf").lower() != lf_now:
            wrong.append("its LF/blob slot reads " + found.group("lf").lower()[:16] + "... and the brief's LF/blob digest is " + lf_now)
        if found.group("raw").lower() != raw_now:
            wrong.append("its working slot reads " + found.group("raw").lower()[:16] + "... and the brief's working digest is " + raw_now)
        if wrong:
            raise Refused(["the new line 1 does not carry the digests of the brief at " + path + ": " + "; ".join(wrong)])
        said = "LINE 1 PLACED IS A HANDOFF head IN THE FORM over " + path + " (LF/blob %s, working %s, re-hashed)" % (lf_now[:8], raw_now[:8])
    if os.path.lexists(temp):
        raise Refused(["a file stands at " + temp + ": it is this tool's one temporary file and its lock, another "
                       "`seat.py head` made it or left it, and it is LEFT AS FOUND"])
    clock = clock_now()
    now_ms = stamp_ms(clock)
    filled = text.replace("{CLOCKMS}", clock)
    spans = ""
    if bases is not None:
        if now_ms < bases[0] or now_ms < bases[1]:
            raise Refused(["a base of the SEAM BASES line is later than the clock at the write (" + clock + ")"])
        first_span, end_span = span_text(bases[0], now_ms), span_text(bases[1], now_ms)
        filled = filled.replace("{SEAM_FROM_FIRST}", first_span).replace("{SEAM_FROM_END}", end_span)
        spans = "; from the first base %s: %s; from the end base %s: %s" % (bases[2], first_span, bases[3], end_span)
    placed = filled.encode("ascii")
    try:
        handle = open(temp, "xb")
    except FileExistsError:
        raise Refused(["a file stands at " + temp + ": it is this tool's one temporary file and its lock, another "
                       "`seat.py head` made it or left it, and it is LEFT AS FOUND"])
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused(["the temporary file " + temp + " could not be made (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + ")"])
    # FROM HERE THE TEMPORARY FILE STANDS. What fails before the replace is a LATE refusal: STATUS.md is not touched,
    # the temporary file is removed, and the line says those two things -- not that nothing was written.
    late, replaced = None, False
    try:
        with handle:
            handle.write(placed + old)
            handle.flush()
            os.fsync(handle.fileno())
        again = read_whole(status)
        if sha256(again) != before:
            late = "STATUS.md moved under this tool between its read and its write (it was sha256 " + before + ")"
        else:
            for attempt in range(5):
                if attempt:
                    time.sleep(0.2)
                try:
                    os.replace(temp, status)
                    replaced = True
                    break
                except PermissionError:
                    late = ("STATUS.md could not be replaced in five tries 200 ms apart (PermissionError: STATUS.md or "
                            "the temporary file is held without sharing delete, or STATUS.md is read-only)")
    except OSError as exc:
        late = "the write did not reach its replace (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + " at " + str(exc.filename or temp) + ")"
    if not replaced:
        gone = False
        for attempt in range(5):
            if attempt:
                time.sleep(0.2)
            try:
                os.remove(temp)
                gone = True
            except FileNotFoundError:
                gone = True
            except OSError:
                continue
            break
        raise Refused([late], tail=(
            "STATUS.md was not touched; the temporary file was written and is removed" if gone else
            "STATUS.md was not touched, AND THE TEMPORARY FILE COULD NOT BE REMOVED in five tries: " + temp + " STANDS, "
            "and every later `seat.py head` at this root is refused until a hand removes it"))
    try:
        new = read_whole(status)
    except OSError as exc:
        # The replace WAS made. The proof is not: said, exit 3 -- never the exit of a finding, never a traceback.
        emit(said)
        emit("PLACED %d line(s) at the head of %s: %d B sha256 %s -> THE REPLACE WAS MADE; new == placed + old: NOT PROVED "
             "(%s: STATUS.md could not be re-read)" % (placed.count(b"\n"), status, len(old), before, exc.__class__.__name__))
        emit("CLOCK " + clock + spans)
        emit("THE ADMISSIONS RECORD: " + ("absent, and not made" if record is None
                                          else "%d line(s), opened for reading alone" % record_lines(record)))
        return 3
    proved = new == placed + old
    emit(said)
    emit("PLACED %d line(s) at the head of %s: %d B sha256 %s -> %d B sha256 %s; new == placed + old: %s" % (
        placed.count(b"\n"), status, len(old), before, len(new), sha256(new), proved))
    emit("CLOCK " + clock + spans)
    emit("THE ADMISSIONS RECORD: " + ("absent, and not made" if record is None
                                      else "%d line(s), opened for reading alone" % record_lines(record)))
    return 0 if proved else 3


def census(root, prefix):
    """The census of one arc's verdict copies, as a dict: every figure, and each table line AS RENDERED."""
    close = os.path.join(root, *CLOSE_PARTS)
    if not os.path.isdir(close):
        raise Refused(["no close folder at " + close])
    try:
        folders = sorted(name for name in os.listdir(close)
                         if name.startswith(prefix) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(close, name)))
        listed = [(folder, sorted(os.listdir(os.path.join(close, folder)))) for folder in folders]
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused(["the close folder at " + close + " cannot be listed (" + exc.__class__.__name__ + " at " +
                       str(exc.filename or close) + ")"])
    stops, strangers, findings, again, seen = [], [], [], [], {}
    for folder, names in listed:
        for name in names:
            path = os.path.join(close, folder, name)
            if not (os.path.isfile(path) and re.match(r"\A.*\.verdict.*\.yaml\Z", name)):
                continue
            data = read_file(path, "verdict copy")
            verdict = parse_verdict(data)
            scalars = verdict["scalars"]
            if "evaluated_at" not in scalars or "verdict" not in scalars:
                strangers.append(folder + "\\" + name)
                continue
            # A STOP IS ONE EVALUATION, AND ITS VERDICT's BYTES ARE ITS OWN: the same bytes met again -- one verdict
            # copied into two folders of the prefix -- are that stop again. It is counted ONCE, under the first copy
            # met in the order of folders and names, and the copy met again is named.
            digest = sha256(data)
            if digest in seen:
                first = seen[digest]
                again.append("%s\\%s (the bytes of %s)" % (folder, name, first["where"]))
                if ("hand-tee-" in name) != first["hand"]:
                    findings.append("%s\\%s: the same verdict is named a %s here and a %s in %s: one stop cannot be "
                                    "both, and its seconds are not in the sum" % (
                                        folder, name, "HAND TEE" if "hand-tee-" in name else "hook stop",
                                        "HAND TEE" if first["hand"] else "hook stop", first["where"]))
                    first["contradicted"] = True
                continue
            seen[digest] = {"where": folder + "\\" + name, "hand": "hand-tee-" in name, "contradicted": False}
            readings = instrument_entries(verdict)
            column = column_word(readings)
            hand = "hand-tee-" in name
            cells, saved = [], []
            for reading in readings:
                if reading["column"] != "REUSED":
                    continue
                if reading["kept_path"] is None:
                    findings.append(folder + "\\" + name + ": REUSED, and the verdict names no kept copy for it")
                    cells.append("-- NO KEPT COPY NAMED; ? s")
                    saved.append(None)
                    continue
                # The kept capture is read ONCE: the bytes its digest was taken over are the bytes its seconds are
                # read from.
                state, _, kept_bytes = kept_on_disk(root, verdict, reading["kept_path"], reading["kept_sha"])
                leaf = re.split(r"[\\/]", reading["kept_path"])[-1]
                elapsed = None
                if state == "EQUAL":
                    for line in text_lines(kept_bytes):
                        if line.startswith("TALLY "):
                            found = ELAPSED_RX.search(line)
                            elapsed = int(found.group(1)) if found else None
                            break
                    if elapsed is None:
                        findings.append(folder + "\\" + name + ": the kept capture " + leaf + " holds no column-0 TALLY line "
                                        "with elapsed_seconds=<n>")
                elif state == "COULD NOT BE OPENED":
                    findings.append(folder + "\\" + name + ": the kept capture " + reading["kept_path"] + " STANDS under "
                                    "--root and COULD NOT BE OPENED in five tries 200 ms apart: it is not read as absent, "
                                    "and its seconds are not in the sum")
                else:
                    findings.append(folder + "\\" + name + ": the kept capture " + reading["kept_path"] + " is " + state +
                                    " under --root at sha256 " + reading["kept_sha"])
                cells.append("`%s` sha256 `%s` -- %s; %s s" % (
                    leaf, reading["kept_sha"],
                    "ON DISK, EQUAL" if state == "EQUAL" else
                    "COULD NOT BE OPENED" if state == "COULD NOT BE OPENED" else "NOT FOUND AT THAT DIGEST",
                    "?" if elapsed is None else str(elapsed)))
                if reading["kept_said"] is not None:
                    # The verdict contradicts itself about WHICH capture was kept: the cell shows the item's capture
                    # as it stands, and its seconds are in no sum -- a finding leaves its stop out, as every other does.
                    findings.append(folder + "\\" + name + ": the detail names another kept path, " + reading["kept_said"] +
                                    ", than the one item of instrument_captures_kept: its seconds are not in the sum")
                    elapsed = None
                saved.append(elapsed)
            # A stop is summed where its COLUMN is REUSED -- every instrument entry reused -- and every capture it
            # cites gave its seconds: then all of them. A stop of entries that differ is MIXED and is not summed.
            seconds = sum(saved) if (column == "REUSED" and saved and None not in saved) else None
            row = (scalars["evaluated_at"], scalars.get("goal", "?"), scalars["verdict"], COLUMN_SHOWN[column],
                   "HAND TEE" if hand else "hook stop",
                   "%s : `%s` %d B sha256 `%s`" % (folder, name, len(data), sha256(data)), " ; ".join(cells))
            stops.append({"row": row, "column": column, "hand": hand, "seconds": seconds, "mark": seen[digest]})
    for stop in stops:
        if stop["mark"]["contradicted"]:
            stop["seconds"] = None
    stops.sort(key=lambda stop: stop["row"])
    hook = [stop for stop in stops if not stop["hand"]]
    tees = [stop for stop in stops if stop["hand"]]
    counts = {word: len([stop for stop in hook if stop["column"] == word]) for word in COLUMN_SHOWN}
    line = "HOOK STOPS REUSED %d / FRESH %d / NOT EVALUATED %d -- %d (unread %d); HAND TEES %d" % (
        counts["REUSED"], counts["FRESH"], counts["NOT_EVALUATED"], len(hook), counts["UNREAD"], len(tees))
    also = ["%s %d" % (COLUMN_SHOWN[word], counts[word]) for word in ("NOT_RUN", "NONE", "MIXED") if counts[word]]
    if also:
        line += " -- also " + ", ".join(also)
    summed = [stop for stop in hook if stop["seconds"] is not None]
    total = sum(stop["seconds"] for stop in summed)
    return {"prefix": prefix, "folders": folders, "copies": len(stops), "hook_stops": len(hook), "hand_tees": len(tees),
            "columns": {COLUMN_SHOWN[word]: counts[word] for word in COLUMN_SHOWN}, "header": CENSUS_HEADER,
            "rule": CENSUS_RULE, "rows": ["| %s | %s | %s | **%s** | %s | %s | %s |" % stop["row"] for stop in stops],
            "line": line, "seconds_saved": total, "reused_hook_stops_summed": len(summed),
            "sum_line": "SECONDS SAVED %d s over %d REUSED hook stop(s)" % (total, len(summed)),
            "not_verdicts": strangers, "same_again": again, "findings": findings}


def run_census(args):
    result = census(os.path.abspath(args.root), args.prefix)
    if args.machine:
        emit(json.dumps(result, ensure_ascii=True, sort_keys=True))
        return 1 if result["findings"] else 0
    emit("THE CENSUS of %d verdict cop%s in %d folder(s) of close/ whose name starts %s (hook stop or HAND TEE by the "
         "file name holding `hand-tee-`: it is recorded nowhere else)" % (
             result["copies"], "y" if result["copies"] == 1 else "ies", len(result["folders"]), ascii(args.prefix)))
    emit(result["header"])
    emit(result["rule"])
    for row in result["rows"]:
        emit(row)
    emit(result["line"])
    emit(result["sum_line"])
    for name in result["same_again"]:
        emit("THE SAME VERDICT AGAIN, counted once: " + name)
    for name in result["not_verdicts"]:
        emit("NOT A VERDICT, counted apart: " + name)
    for finding in result["findings"]:
        emit("FINDING: " + finding)
    return 1 if result["findings"] else 0


def main(argv):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="seat.py", description="The seating helper: the verdict copy and its "
                                     "statement, the keep-table compare, the STATUS head, the stops by column.")
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="command")
    p_copy = sub.add_parser("copy", help="copy the goal's verdict into one close folder, named by its bytes")
    p_copy.add_argument("--root", required=True, help="the mission root")
    p_copy.add_argument("--goal", required=True, help="the goal id")
    p_copy.add_argument("--close-folder", required=True, help="the folder under .mission-runtime/lam/close")
    p_copy.add_argument("--verdict", default=None, help="the verdict file, where both places hold one")
    p_copy.add_argument("--hand-tee", default=None, help="a label: the copy is a hand tee's, and is named so")
    p_copy.add_argument("--make-folder", action="store_true", help="make the one close folder where it is absent")
    p_read = sub.add_parser("read", help="print what a verdict is, by its bytes; write nothing")
    p_read.add_argument("--root", required=True, help="the mission root the verdict's runtime plane is read under")
    which = p_read.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    which.add_argument("--goal", default=None, help="the goal id")
    which.add_argument("--verdict", default=None, help="a verdict file or a copy of one")
    p_keep = sub.add_parser("keep", help="compare a brief's keep-table with a copy folder")
    p_keep.add_argument("--brief", required=True, help="the brief that holds the table")
    p_keep.add_argument("--copy", required=True, help="the folder the table's files are looked for in")
    p_keep.add_argument("--exclude", action="append", default=None, help="a top-level folder of the copy the table leaves out")
    p_head = sub.add_parser("head", help="prepend a head to STATUS.md, every prior byte kept beneath it")
    p_head.add_argument("--root", required=True, help="the mission root")
    p_head.add_argument("--line-file", required=True, help="the head's lines: ASCII, LF, one or more")
    mode = p_head.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    mode.add_argument("--replace-handoff", action="store_true", help="line 1 is a HANDOFF head; place a plain one over it")
    mode.add_argument("--place-handoff", action="store_true", help="place a HANDOFF head whose digests are the brief's")
    p_head.add_argument("--predecessor-brief", default=None, help="the brief whose SEAM BASES line the spans are read from")
    p_head.add_argument("--expect-sha256", default=None, help="the sha256 STATUS.md must have before the write")
    p_census = sub.add_parser("census", help="the arc's verdict copies by column, and the seconds REUSED saved")
    p_census.add_argument("--root", required=True, help="the mission root")
    p_census.add_argument("--prefix", required=True, help="the close folders' prefix, e.g. arc-pb-5-")
    p_census.add_argument("--machine", action="store_true", help="one JSON object: the fields and each line as rendered")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    runs = {"copy": run_copy, "read": run_read, "keep": run_keep, "head": run_head, "census": run_census}
    if args.command not in runs:
        parser.print_usage(sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        return runs[args.command](args)
    except Refused as exc:
        emit("REFUSED: " + "; ".join(exc.reasons) + " -- " + (exc.tail or "nothing was written"))
        return 2
    except OSError as exc:
        # No verb writes after an open it did not guard, so what reaches here was met at a read or a listing: it is
        # said as a refusal, by name, and never as a traceback under the exit of a finding.
        emit("REFUSED: " + exc.__class__.__name__ + " at " + str(exc.filename or "a path the system does not name") +
             " -- this run stopped there, and wrote nothing after it")
        return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
